Objective

Investigate approaches for maintaining an accurate Snyk Production lifecycle across all application teams while reducing manual effort and improving reporting consistency.

This spike evaluates several approaches to ensure that only the current production codebase is represented as the Snyk Production project.

Background

Currently, Snyk Production lifecycle assignments are inconsistent across applications.

Some application teams assign the Production lifecycle directly to release branches, resulting in multiple production targets over time.

Example:

release/2026.06  → Production
release/2026.07  → Production
release/2026.08  → Production

This creates several operational challenges:

Multiple projects representing Production
Inconsistent monthly reporting
Difficulty determining which project represents the live production deployment
Manual lifecycle management
Problem Statement

The current process lacks a standardized approach for identifying the production branch monitored by Snyk.

Different applications use different branching strategies, resulting in inconsistent Production lifecycle assignments.

The objective of this spike is to determine the most scalable approach for standardizing Production monitoring across application teams.

Requirements

The proposed solution should:

Maintain a single Production lifecycle target per application
Continue scanning release branches before production deployment
Support existing application branching strategies where possible
Minimize manual lifecycle management
Improve reporting consistency
Be scalable across all application teams
