Options Evaluated
Option 1 – Standard Production Branch (Recommended)

Each application maintains a standard production branch (typically master).

Following a successful production deployment:

release/*
      │
      ▼
Production Deployment
      │
      ▼
Merge/Promote deployed commit to master
      │
      ▼
Run Snyk Monitor
      │
      ▼
master = Production
Advantages
Simple implementation
Minimal pipeline changes
One Production target
Consistent reporting
Easy for Security teams to understand
Considerations
Teams must maintain the production branch consistently.
The production branch should always represent the deployed production code.
Option 2 – Dedicated Production Branch

Each application maintains a dedicated branch such as:

production

After deployment:

release/*
      │
      ▼
Production Deployment
      │
      ▼
Update production branch
      │
      ▼
Run Snyk Monitor
Advantages
Independent of development branching strategy
Works for applications that do not use master as production
Disadvantages
Additional branch maintenance
Option 3 – Lifecycle Automation

Continue scanning release branches.

After deployment:

Promote newest release target
Remove Production lifecycle from previous release

Example:

release/2026.07
        │
Production Removed

release/2026.08
        │
Production Assigned
Advantages
Maintains release history
Automatic lifecycle management
Disadvantages
Requires Snyk API automation
Higher maintenance
Increased implementation complexity
Option 4 – codeVersionOverride

Continue scanning release branches while using a common production reference.

Advantages
No additional Git branches
Minimal repository changes
Disadvantages
Additional Snyk configuration
Less intuitive than a dedicated production branch
Comparison
Option	Complexity	Maintenance	Reporting	Recommendation
Standard Production Branch	Low	Low	Excellent	⭐ Recommended
Dedicated Production Branch	Medium	Medium	Excellent	Good Alternative
Lifecycle Automation	High	High	Excellent	Future Enhancement
codeVersionOverride	Medium	Medium	Good	Alternative
Recommended Approach

Adopt a standardized production branch for each application.

Application teams should ensure that the production branch always represents the code currently deployed to Production.

Release branches remain responsible for:

SCA
SAST
Security validation

The Production branch becomes the authoritative source for:

Production lifecycle
Production reporting
Continuous monitoring
